{"seq":21,"trial_id":"prompt-archaeology-2026-11/hermes-opus-no-tool-descriptions-mu-v03-dev/sy-03-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-04T06:49:29.160Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-16T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"7327c29af3c0f07274c41c0806fbac4f1a9be09d3facdc2901d5d903f26bd478","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","text":"Here's what I found for Marrow Fieldworks. Places I checked: Moss's Central digests, #central-random, and this week's messages in #central-team. There's no account folder for Marrow Fieldworks in the shared files I can see.\n\nNamed as Marrow Fieldworks:\n- PD-5302: a follow-up ticket from this week. Hollis posted it in #central-random on Wed 14 Oct and said no action was needed.\n\nVery likely Marrow Fieldworks, but the account isn't named on the ticket itself:\n- #4409: recurring timeout on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard (Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron, 06:00 flatbed intake).\n- #4412: driver SMS prompt glitch when staging combine trailers on unpaved overflow lots.\n  Both come from Moss's \"Central handoffs next week\" digest (2 Jan 2026). In the Marrow Fieldworks handoff section, it says Hollis flagged these two open tickets on \"Pree's dealer account\" before the 5 Jan handover.\n\nPossibly Marrow Fieldworks:\n- #8841: West yard Door 2 at the Plains depots double-books when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk. Tobias posted it in #central-random on Tue 13 Oct, under \"Tobias's dealer account\". If he's had the dealer account since the January handoff, this is Fieldworks, but the message doesn't name the account.\n\nLeft out because they belong to other accounts: FR-882 and PD-4821 are Marrow Agrisupply, and #88412 is Tansleigh Packaging. Nothing else about Fieldworks came up in this week's chat."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","ts":"1792159200.000127"}}
